!!! When a file was last written.
!!!
!!! nil.std.io had a size and no timestamp, which left two ordinary jobs
!!! unreachable: a cache could not tell whether what it held was still
!!! current without re-reading the file, and an HTTP server could not send
!!! Last-Modified or answer If-Modified-Since.
!!!
!!! Nothing here can assert a particular instant. What it asserts is that the
!!! answer is a plausible epoch time in milliseconds, that writing again
!!! moves it forward rather than back, and that an absent file is reported
!!! rather than given a zero that a comparison would read as 1970.

book matrix.file-time

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.io.file

stamp-of receives path as text returns number begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.io::modified_at with path being path
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding stamped then give stamped
        otherwise give 0 minus 1
    end consider
end paragraph

main returns number begin paragraph
    value path is "matrix-file-time-fixture.txt"
    evaluate nil.std.io::write_text with path being path, content being "first"
    value first-stamp is stamp-of with path being path

    !!! Milliseconds since the Unix epoch, so any real file is well past the
    !!! start of 2020 and well short of the year 2200. A seconds-based answer
    !!! would fail the lower bound, which is the mistake worth catching.
    say (first-stamp is greater than 1577836800000) becomes text
    say (first-stamp is less than 7258118400000) becomes text

    evaluate nil.std.io::write_text with path being path, content being "second and longer"
    value second-stamp is stamp-of with path being path
    say (second-stamp is at least first-stamp) becomes text

    !!! The size moved too, which is what a validator pairs with the time.
    value measured is nil.std.io::size with path being path
    consider measured
        when Result.Ok holding width then say width
        otherwise say 0 minus 1
    end consider

    evaluate nil.std.io::delete with path being path
    !!! An absent file is reported, not given a zero that a comparison would
    !!! read as the epoch and treat as very old indeed.
    say stamp-of with path being path
    give 0
end paragraph
